From d7e7e0c2e2b3b90e81df2cd03cad943ad2ae95a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:41:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 150/155] network: add an uplink address resolver

A host with more than one uplink chooses between them by binding an
outgoing socket to a local address, which the kernel then matches
against its source routing rules. Nothing in Kodi can express that
choice today.

Resolve it from a specification that is stable across a lease renewal:
an address, a subnet, or an interface name, looked up when the socket is
about to be opened rather than when the setting is written. The lookup
goes through getifaddrs() because CNetwork's interface list is built
once at startup and drops interfaces without a hardware address, which
is exactly what a tunnel looks like.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 xbmc/network/CMakeLists.txt    |   2 +
 xbmc/network/UplinkAddress.cpp | 106 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/network/UplinkAddress.h   |  19 ++++++
 3 files changed, 127 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/network/UplinkAddress.cpp
 create mode 100644 xbmc/network/UplinkAddress.h

--- a/xbmc/network/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/xbmc/network/CMakeLists.txt
